ick  in here but many people believe the  goddess of time is the Forgotten fourth  sister of the three golden goddesses who  created the world while I won't go too  far into this and you know the whole  theory of the tetra force and stuff like  that it could be that since didn't  create  the earth nehru created the law of the  world and for Rory created life the  fourth sister the goddess of time could  have created time and therefore the day  and night cycle represented by the Sun  but contrasted by the moon it seems like  the people of the land of termina  knowingly accept the existence of the  goddess of time and pairing that  knowledge with the fourth Triforce piece  represented on the Hylian Shield from  ocarina of time  definitely implies the validation of  this theory furthermore since the fourth  piece which in this case is representing  the goddess of time is both separated  from the other three pieces and also  inverted it could imply that the goddess  is against the other three which melds  well with the notion that the Blood Moon  aka the goddess of time assists ganon  and his Wiles another piece of evidence  that the goddess of time is a golden  goddess herself is the fact that she  also has a spiritual stone the moon's  tear could it be that the moon is either  being forced to or willingly is  partnered with Ganon and could this help  explain the strange backwards melody in  breath of the wild twos trailer is  Ganondorf being rewound back to life of  course if I follow this rabbit trail too  far I'll get into all sorts of stuff  like where's the wielder of the fourth  tetra force piece so I'll stop that  theory there and get back on track now  the next possibility is that the moon is  whatever demon or dark God resides in  the dark got a statue outside Hatano  village though I'd say I don't  personally believe this one due to the  nature and personality of the statues  resident I don't know I just can't see  it that guy's too funny but finally it  could always be a new unknown demon that  demise either created or cursed the moon  with way back in the days before ocarina  of time this would explain why the moon  seems to hold the power of Resurrection  over the dead even when it's set in a  universe without Ganon such as termina  implying the power over the undead was  given to the moon and not to Ganon but  of course this is all now in the realm  of speculation and on that note what do  you think let me know in a comment below  hey guys thank you so much for watching  my crazy theory please be sure to  subscribe with that Bell icon if you  haven't already to stick around for all  the juicy Nintendo content right here at  mass antennae bandit and also like this  video if you enjoyed it to spread the  love as always humongous thank you to  all of my amazing patrons who make my  day  everyday if you're interested in getting  your name up here at the end of all of  my videos check out the links in the  description below for more info also  down there are the links to my social  media pages and hey don't forget about  the competition that's ending really  soon  that's all I've got for this video so I  hope you have a great rest of your day  this is Mastana Bandits signing out  peace  [Music]

